<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ new dwelling estimates fall 3.7 pct in Sept yr.</title>
<headline>NZ new dwelling estimates fall 3.7 pct in Sept yr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand provisional figures show 1,694 new dwelling units were authorised for construction in Setpember, 3.7 percent fewer than in September 1995, Statistics New Zealand said on Friday.</p>
<p>It said the trend esimate fell 4.5 percent from August to Setpmber. It said the trend reached a peak in April 1996 and had been declining since.  </p>
<p>The largest increases in the year were for North Shore City, up to 119 from 83, Hamilton, up to 88 from 64, and Auckland to 106 from 90.</p>
<p>The largest decreases were for Waitakere, down to 91 from 137, Manukau to 126 from 157 and Kapiti to 32 from 60.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
